    "created_at": "2017-11-23T08:46:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-11-23T08:46:57Z",
    "body": "Given how rel=icon and the manifest feed into the same processing model in most implementations, I think if we want to solve this, we should make sure we have parity across both the manifest and the link tag representations.\r\n\r\nAs for whether we want to, I'm unsure. It seems at least we'd need to do *something* different this time around if we're to avoid just going through the same cycle manifest did and removing it after implementations notice that respecting the parameter gives bad results. I don't know what we could do though.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
